# traffic-one — Core (framework-agnostic)

Project-level conventions for any TypeScript project. Stack-specific rules live in
`react-core.mdc` (React web) or `react-native-core.mdc` (Expo React Native).

## Language
- **TypeScript ^5** — never plain JS for new files.
- `tsconfig` baseline: `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noImplicitOverride`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `verbatimModuleSyntax`.
- No `any` — `unknown` and narrow.
- Discriminated unions over flag + optional combos.
- Infer types from schemas (zod, valibot).

## Workspace
- **Monorepo:** Turborepo + pnpm workspaces.
- Shared code in `packages/*`; never duplicate utilities across apps.
- Cross-package imports use workspace package names — never deep relative paths.

## File & function size
- 200–400 lines per file (800 hard cap). Functions ≤ 50 lines, single responsibility.

## Validation & errors
- Validate every external input at the boundary with a typed schema.
- Map transport errors to a typed `AppError` discriminated union.
- Handle errors explicitly at every layer.

## Git — Gitflow
- Branches: `main` / `develop` / `feature/*` / `release/*` / `hotfix/*`.
- Conventional commits with ticket id in scope; subject ≤ 72 chars.

## Tooling
- Husky + lint-staged. Commitlint with conventional rules.
- Lockfile committed; `pnpm audit` in CI.
